  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOL: Enhance capacities of care workers to support children separated from their families</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support the implementation of 2022-2026 National Child Protection programme, through: 1) addressing a capacity gap in the social protection system, especially social workers&#x2019; capacities to conduct comprehensive children&#x2019; families&#x2019; and services&#x2019; assessment in the context of ensuring the right of every child to grow up in safe and nurturing family environment and following assessment to develop individual plans for children who are currently in Chisinau Institution for babies and young children (est. 20 children and their families) and 2) to enhance the skills and knowledge of 30 foster carers in 9 counties who look after over 98 children who lived through adverse childhood experiences. The priority will be offered to the foster families who have in placement children 2-7 years old. Foster carers will be supported to acquire and apply skills to enhance the relationship between children and adults as a strategy to understand and decrease the risks of conduct disorders, to reduce challenging behaviours and to promote and encourage positive behaviour. In addition, foster care managers from 9 counties will strengthen their knowledge of the CARE methodology for future monitoring. The foster parents and the specialists have been trained in a 6 hours training in 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
